  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The state recorded $19.2B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Obligations fell 28.7% year over year. The state logged 387,009 awards with an average award size of $49.6K. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer with $15.3B in obligations, followed by the Department of Energy with $2B. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is the largest industry by dollars at $4.5B, and Medicinal and Botanical Manufacturing follows with $3.3B. AMERISOURCEBERGEN DRUG CORP received the most obligations at $4.8B, followed by FLUOR MARINE PROPULSION, LLC at $4B and BECHTEL PLANT MACHINERY, INC. at $2.1B. Fiscal-year trends show higher totals in prior years, including $26.9B in FY25 and $26.6B in FY24, with the current fiscal year to date total below those levels. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial for the fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has federal contracting in Pennsylvania changed year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 28.7% year over year. Total obligations are $19.2B for FY2026 to date, down from prior fiscal-year totals such as $26.9B in FY25 and $26.6B in FY24. The award count is 387,009 and the average award size is $49.6K, reflecting the current-year-to-date activity level."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries dominate federal spending in Pennsylvania?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense awarded $15.3B, making it the largest buying agency in the state. The Department of Energy awarded $2B and the Department of Veterans Affairs awarded $641M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is the largest industry at $4.5B, with Medicinal and Botanical Manufacturing at $3.3B and Power Boiler and Heat Exchanger Manufacturing at $2.1B."
      }
    ]
